| `scripts/expiring_tier_data.py` | Holds `CEILING`, the latest date `expiring_tier.expires` may hold, and `CHECKS`, each check id that adopts the tier mapped to its gate test's node id. It is data, not logic (CONVENTIONS §18), and keel owns it, so copier rewrites it on every update. | imported by `scripts/expiring_tier.py` and `scripts/record_gate_baseline.py` | — | Nothing inside a repository stops a determined edit of it: a project's edit shows as a diff or a conflict on the next update. Not the project's own date: that is `expiring_tier.expires`. | [generate-and-upgrade.md](../guides/generate-and-upgrade.md) | always |
